## July's Notable Recalls  
### 1. MOGO Moringa LLC  
**Reason:** Salmonella contamination  
**Product Details:** MOGO PURE MORINGA OLEIFERA CAPSULES  
This Class I recall highlights the significant risks associated with contamination in dietary supplements.  
---
### 2. Western Mixers Produce & Nuts, Inc.  
**Reason:** Undeclared peanuts  
**Product Details:** FIRST STREET Dark Chocolate Raisins  
Undeclared allergens remain a top concern, posing life-threatening risks to consumers.  
---
### 3. NARA ORGANICS INC  
**Reason:** Potential Clostridium botulinum contamination  
**Product Details:** nara organics; Whole Milk Organic Infant Formula  
A Class I recall with potential fatal consequences, particularly concerning given that the product is for infants.  
## The Usual Suspects  
Spring & Mulberry Inc. continues to top the list of worst offenders with 11 Class I recalls. Consumer trust in their products remains highly questionable.  
## Monthly Trends and Observations  
Recalls are on the rise, with a significant spike in June (212 cases). This demands scrutiny towards manufacturers and the FDA's regulatory oversight.  
